WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.706
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.706 --> 00:00:05.387
- I'm one of the few
people you will ever meet

00:00:05.387 --> 00:00:07.708
in your whole life, who is impervious

00:00:07.708 --> 00:00:10.152
to the pain caused by eating too much ice.

00:00:10.152 --> 00:00:11.343
- What?
- Whoa...

00:00:11.343 --> 00:00:12.605
- I just like ice.

00:00:12.605 --> 00:00:14.143
(laughing)

00:00:14.143 --> 00:00:15.889
- This is the kind of ice they use

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:18.105
to pad your drinks and you get less soda.

00:00:18.105 --> 00:00:19.319
- Yeah, you want something that just

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:20.442
really crumbles in your mouth.

00:00:20.442 --> 00:00:22.058
- It's the kind of ice
that just sticks together.

00:00:22.058 --> 00:00:23.530
Look at that.
- Is this gas station ice?

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:25.677
- [Everyone] Oooh

00:00:25.677 --> 00:00:27.827
- This is some hot ice right here.

00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:30.452
- This is some top shelf.
- It's like snow.

00:00:30.452 --> 00:00:32.442
- They're easy to chew.
- Helluva crunch.

00:00:32.442 --> 00:00:33.496
- They're just nice to look at.

00:00:33.496 --> 00:00:34.745
- They're all perfectly round.

00:00:34.745 --> 00:00:37.235
- I gotta say though, it
still does the clumping thing.

00:00:37.235 --> 00:00:39.582
Where it all at once freezes together,

00:00:39.582 --> 00:00:40.383
and hits you in the face.

00:00:40.383 --> 00:00:41.633
- Doesn't all ice do that?

00:00:41.633 --> 00:00:42.882
- No.
- No.

00:00:42.882 --> 00:00:43.694
- What?
- Carol!

00:00:43.694 --> 00:00:45.135
- [Everyone] Oh...

00:00:45.135 --> 00:00:46.089
- Oh yeah...

00:00:46.089 --> 00:00:47.715
- Did little-itty-bitty-mini cubes

00:00:47.715 --> 00:00:49.927
- But are they small enough?
- This is pretty good.

00:00:49.927 --> 00:00:52.665
- This is in between a
good cube and a round ice.

00:00:52.665 --> 00:00:53.719
- And it sounds really good.

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:54.928
(ice rattling)

00:00:54.928 --> 00:00:56.187
- It's the kind that when
you are using a straw,

00:00:56.187 --> 00:00:58.371
it gets stuck.
- Good point.

00:00:58.371 --> 00:01:00.232
- Right. I'm mad when that happens.

00:01:00.232 --> 00:01:01.856
- [Man in blue shirt] Awe.

00:01:01.856 --> 00:01:04.070
- This is easily the best of all the ices.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:05.521
- I can't put this in my mouth.

00:01:05.521 --> 00:01:08.227
- That's not the point.
It cools your whiskey.

00:01:08.227 --> 00:01:11.094
- It does. It melts it at a good rate.

00:01:11.094 --> 00:01:12.624
- But it also doesn't
water down your whiskey.

00:01:12.624 --> 00:01:13.701
- It doesn't.
- It's not edible.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.751
- This is bull****.
- Not edible?

00:01:15.751 --> 00:01:19.465
What are you, six? This makes
me want whiskey right now.

00:01:19.465 --> 00:01:22.948
- [Everyone] Hey cheers guys, cheers.

00:01:22.948 --> 00:01:25.993
- Mmm
(red haired woman laughing)

00:01:25.993 --> 00:01:27.503
- I feel like ******* Frank Sinatra.

00:01:27.503 --> 00:01:29.303
- This is some grown-up-ass ice.

00:01:29.303 --> 00:01:31.223
- I was not happy.

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:32.686
- [Everyone] Ooh!

00:01:32.686 --> 00:01:35.347
- What is this?
- Why is it so hard?

00:01:35.347 --> 00:01:37.145
Look at it, it doesn't
even have any shape.

00:01:37.145 --> 00:01:38.690
- What a deceptive ice.
- Wow.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:40.020
- I don't know. Where is this from?

00:01:40.020 --> 00:01:42.232
But they've perfected the round cube.

00:01:42.232 --> 00:01:43.942
- It was from the gutter,
is where it's from.

00:01:43.942 --> 00:01:47.115
- Ooh! Do you hate it so much?
- I hate this ice.

00:01:47.715 --> 00:01:49.114
- [Man in blue shirt] Whoa.

00:01:49.114 --> 00:01:51.345
- McDonald's ice was garbage.

00:01:51.345 --> 00:01:52.995
- [Red-haired woman] Too hard, too hard.

00:01:52.995 --> 00:01:54.691
- In the commercials
it looks great though.

00:01:54.691 --> 00:01:56.581
- Yeah, I thought Sonic
was better than that.

00:01:56.581 --> 00:01:58.247
- (Red-haired woman) Yes....

00:01:58.247 --> 00:02:00.746
I mean, you know, you gotta sometimes

00:02:00.746 --> 00:02:03.097
think about what the ice feels in.

00:02:03.097 --> 00:02:04.545
- Ella, that was super-philosophical.

00:02:04.545 --> 00:02:06.130
- [Man in blue shirt] They agree with you.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:07.755
Those are great.
- Those are good.

00:02:07.755 --> 00:02:09.591
- That was just Chick-Fil-A?

00:02:09.591 --> 00:02:13.360
- [Everyone] Yeah!

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.763
- We all knew, we all knew.
- Yes.

00:02:15.763 --> 00:02:17.266
- This blows my mind because the

00:02:17.266 --> 00:02:18.892
context of that ice is so different.

00:02:18.892 --> 00:02:20.355
that's being used.
- That's coffee.

00:02:20.355 --> 00:02:21.563
- See that changes the whole game.

00:02:21.563 --> 00:02:23.311
The best ice is ice
that never gets noticed.

00:02:23.311 --> 00:02:24.611
- Yeah
- Mmm

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:27.366
- What a thankless job ice has.

00:02:27.366 --> 00:02:28.824
- It turns out that I have lots

00:02:28.824 --> 00:02:31.349
of strong feelings about ice
that I never talked about.

00:02:31.349 --> 00:02:33.349
- I feel like most people do.

